  "scope": "Public Robinhood read path. Static assets, boot/auth/session/receipt requests, optional pool-detail diagnostics, background collectors and retries/failover are identified separately.",
  "assumptions": [
    "One visible tab per modeled concurrent user; composition 80% Home/selected Markets/PoolDetail, 10% ready token explorer, 10% other screens.",
    "Fast overview polling rounded conservatively to 12/min; actual timer is 5s plus request duration, and Home/Markets adds 0-10% jitter.",
    "Successful requests, no retries/failover, normal ERC20 contracts, healthy local v4 primary.",
    "Each modeled wallet page has 20 distinct ERC20 candidates and no extra explicit addresses; empty/smaller pages cost less.",
    "Each modeled NFT lookup has two live IDs. Uncached token metadata from NFT or other screens is included in A, not counted again.",
    "Alchemy inventory remains intentional and exclusively Alchemy; generic Robinhood reads use local primary with configured fallback.",
    "Rates are offered demand, not accepted throughput or measured capacity.",
    "Optional enabledReads in production are not inferred from the disabled candidate wrangler file."
  ],
  "variables": {
    "M": "Fraction visible on fast-overview pages",
